    "volume_basis": "Table 1 conventional hexagonal unit-cell volume V=(sqrt(3)/2)*a^2*c; the MgSiO3 ilmenite cell has Z=6.",
    "temperature_ref": "The experiment and EOS are reported at ambient temperature; 298 K is the operational ambient-temperature reference used by this record."
   },
   "notes": "This is the authors' preferred pressure assignment of the same experiment represented by the companion ruby-scale record. It is a distinct fit, not a duplicate parameter transcription. Ice-VII (110) diffraction and MgSiO3 ilmenite were measured on the same 50 micrometer X-ray spot; Table 1 prints 12 finite-pressure Pi values, and Figure 3f additionally plots the two ambient measurements as zero-pressure anchors, giving 14 usable rows. The paper reports that V0 was varied and K0 was fixed at the adopted 212 GPa Brillouin value. Above 15 GPa the pressure medium developed nonhydrostatic stress and pressure gradients; the bracketed ice-pressure quantities are maximum gradient estimates, not stated one-sigma errors. The source gives neither parameter covariance nor a confidence convention for fitted-parameter errors. The numerical 298 K reference encodes the source's qualitative 'ambient temperature' wording rather than a measured sample temperature.",
